seg-7b56ed698c30 = Four scenario kinds, each also a phase kind of the <c1/> interface (<c2/>): they carry a navigation-and-timing error budget through a south-polar lunar mission, from rendezvous in lunar orbit to landing, the surface stay and the ascent back to orbit. <b>Every number here is MODELLED</b>: a stated model with ILLUSTRATIVE inputs, none of it a statement about any mission, system or site. "Artemis-class" names a class of mission concept, nothing more; no agency's data, product or endorsement is used or claimed, and nothing here is affiliated with one. Advisory software, not certified navigation equipment. Kshana transmits nothing and drives no hardware.

