seg-5d3fa3e8486c = <b>What the result says.</b> With signals alone, the crosslink range fixes the relative position along the line of sight, but the relative position across it is limited by the independent signal-in-space error and by what the dynamics give; docking needs a relative sensor, and the <c1/> rows show at what range each of the thread's sensor models beats the signals. The result also depends on the truth and the estimator sharing a force model; the <c2/> estimator option shows the cost of ignoring the harmonics, and that run is not expected to be consistent.

